const route2 = flow('LR', [['s', 'Standard derivatives'], ['c', 'Chain rule'], ['a', '$a^x$ and logarithms'], ['i', 'Inverse trigonometric derivatives'], ['t', 'Trigonometric substitution']], [['s', 'c'], ['c', 'a'], ['a', 'i'], ['i', 't']], 'Route map of Part 2: standard derivatives, the chain rule, exponentials with any base and logarithms, inverse trigonometric derivatives, and trigonometric substitution.', 'Part 2 at a glance.');
const stdD = table(['$f(x)$', "$f'(x)$", '$f(x)$', "$f'(x)$"], [['$\\sin x$', '$\\cos x$', '$e^x$', '$e^x$'], ['$\\cos x$', '$-\\sin x$', '$a^x$', '$a^x\\log a$'], ['$\\tan x$', '$\\sec^2 x$', '$\\log x$', '$\\dfrac{1}{x}$'], ['$\\sec x$', '$\\sec x\\tan x$', '$\\operatorname{cosec} x$', '$-\\operatorname{cosec} x\\cot x$']], 'Table of standard derivatives: sine to cosine, cosine to minus sine, tangent to secant squared, secant to secant tangent, e to the x to itself, a to the x to a to the x times log a, log x to 1 over x, cosec to minus cosec cot.', 'Learn these by heart; the chain rule does the rest.');
